00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.510 align:start position:0%
 
so one of the biggest questions that  fans have had since the hogwarts legacy  gameplay revealed back in march will we  be able to play quidditch and today i'm  reporting that according to multiple  sources close to the project hogwarts  legacy will not feature playable  quidditch please donate the messenger  guys and honestly don't hate on  avalanche either i understand it i'll  explain why now i'm sure you all have so  many questions so i'm going to try and  answer several of what i anticipate will  be the most frequently asked questions  i'll also explain why i'm personally  okay with this decision here in a bit  but first i think it's important to note  this does not mean quidditch will be  completely absent from the world in  hogwarts legacy i mean it's not like  they're going to pretend it doesn't  exist or something i mean if you think  back to the gameplay reveal trailer it  clearly shows the quidditch pitch and  what appears to be characters wearing  quidditch robes then you have the asmr  video which also gave us a look at  quality quidditch supplies so quidditch  will still be part of this world it may  even factor into the story we may even  see people playing quidditch i don't  know what i'm confirming today though is  that it will not be playable for our  character alright so let's try and  tackle some of those questions that i  know you have and i expect the biggest  one to be why why would they not include  quidditch well if you go back to the  2020 blog post from adrian rob he said  quote often the difficult task is  choosing which details we aren't going  to explore close quote i honestly think  it was simply a matter of managing the  resources and trying to decide what all  they wanted to include from the  wizarding world simply because there is  so much it's such a deep and rich world  some sacrifices had to be made in  another blog post from community manager  chandler wood he said he asked game  director alan tu what fans love and  expect from the wizarding world and that  their resulting conversations could fill  tomes because of the sheer amount of  everything that could be included then  chandler goes on to try and get him to  narrow it down to just two sentences and  two told him quote the most ever-present  part of the wizarding world is its magic  and the playful nature and realness of  its distinct rules should fuel a  surprising dark mystery that tests the  combined resources of those who discover  it but just as important are the  opportunities to experience hundreds of  memorable moments small and large that  fans grew up with and know by heart from  being sorted in the great hall exploring  a new secret chamber in hogwarts or  impersonating others with polyjuice  potion to protecting innocents from a  dangerous troll dodging fireballs from a  hungarian horntail or soaring into the  sky on the back of a friendly hippogriff  i mean that is one heck of a list right  there guys and seemingly confirmation  that we're gonna get all of those or  something close to that in hogwarts  legacy and really this is part of the  reason that i'm okay with this decision  and i understand it trust me i know  there are a lot of you out there who are  going to be really upset by this who  really wanted quidditch trust me i get  it but think about it like this for a  second would you really have wanted them  to devote a ton of time and resources to  focusing on quidditch which was big  enough to get its own full game back  with harry potter quidditch world cup  years ago when they could instead be  focusing on perfecting say the spell  casting system or fleshing out more  story details what about adding more  hidden passages in hogwarts or working  on the vendors and cosmetic upgrades in  hogsmeade i mean as much as i love  quidditch there are plenty of other  things on that list that i think are  much more important and i think as fans  we just have to trust that this is going  to make for a better overall game as it  does allow avalanche to focus on the  most important parts of an action rpg  which let's be honest here the story the  spells the gameplay mechanics of spell  casting the collectibles side quest  hogwarts itself and all of the secrets  are just far more important than  including playable quidditch which truth  be told would really be a side activity  that not even everyone would want to  participate in i mean let's try and  think about it like this if they did try  and include playable quidditch then they  would have to make even more sacrifices  like is it part of the story to have the  player character participate or do we  make it a completely optional thing and  if it's only optional then how do we  really justify spending a lot of time  and resources on this should they force  them into the secret position like we  did with harry or do they try and  include all the positions do they have a  quidditch cup that sets matches against  other houses i mean the list goes on and  on another question i expect to get on  this is how sure i am and can i reveal  the sources i would say i'm about 98  sure barring something drastic changing  i'm about 98 sure that this will be true  i'm very confident in these sources and  no unfortunately i cannot disclose them  that's just not how this works guys and  if you choose not to believe look  totally okay by me i get it you're right  to be skeptical i'm not an ign i'm not a  gamestop i'm just a dad who loves games  and the stories they tell another  expected question do i think there's  still time to add quidditch or could we  get it later on so definite no on the  first one but on the second one i'll say  maybe in that blog post i mentioned alan  2 had a line near the end where he said  with your continued support we hope to  explore even more in the future as soon  as i read that it immediately sounded to  me like the possibility of dlc and maybe  even sequel so i do think and this is  purely me guessing here no sources or  anything on this i do think if this game  is successful and they continue to hear  a strong fan desire for quidditch they  could very well look into adding it  later down the line maybe as post-launch  dlc i mean we do have to remember we  know that flying on a broom is 100 for  sure in the game so they would already  have that kind of bass line to help them  if they wanted to build a quidditch game  on top of that but then we get into that  question of resources again would fans  really want an added quidditch mode more  so than say a new story dlc i mean if  i'm wb i think these are all things that  they would be listening to if this game  is successful which i think it will be  they're going to be listening to the  fans what are the fans want more of what  are the fans want out of hogwarts legacy  do the fans want a completely new game  who knows maybe someone would even  consider a brand new quidditch world cup  game if there's enough demand honestly  this would be my personal preference i  would love if a developer whether it's  avalanche or someone else was given the  proper time and care to be able to make  a fully developed standalone quidditch  game with multiplayer i'd much prefer  that in sort of a small tact on mode to  hogwarts legacy but i mean i could see  it going either way depending on the fan  reaction and fan response now while  today's news story answers one of the  big questions that we still had about  the game there are still plenty that we  don't know the answer to in fact i've  already made a video on the top  questions that i still have for hogwarts  legacy you can check it out on the right  side of your screen now as always thank  you all so much for watching i'll talk  to you again soon

